2026-11-13T00:00:00Z (RFD66606-2493) 'a zone relay only routes
 # uuid: 2a868d5c-b3cd-579e-b4bd-b196fa5cc78c
 # tags: rfd:title, rfd:flight-level:l1
 RFD:Discussion  1 RFD
 Serials:VSekaiFabric

2026-11-13T00:00:01Z (RFD66606-2493) 'a zone hands each member the others' frames and reads none of them.
 # tags: rfd:feature, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:02Z (RFD66606-2493) 'the presence slice's zone relay: its rule for taking a frame, its sockets, its gates.
 # tags: rfd:scope, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:03Z (RFD66606-2493) 'Can a zone carry four people's bodies to each other without simulating, decoding or judging
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:04Z (RFD66606-2493) 'anything, and without trusting the clock of anyone who sends to it?
 # tags: rfd:hook
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:05Z (RFD66606-2493) 'A zone that simulates is one more party to trust. The first relay built here avoided that and
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:06Z (RFD66606-2493) 'still trusted something it should not have: it opened each sender's turn on a tick of its own
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:07Z (RFD66606-2493) 'clock. Run on real sockets for the first time, it refused 7 honest frames of 320. A client's
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:08Z (RFD66606-2493) 'clock is not the relay's, and a send that drifts across the relay's tick lands twice in one
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:09Z (RFD66606-2493) 'turn and not at all in the next. The model's gate had passed, because its clients and its
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:10Z (RFD66606-2493) 'router shared one clock.
 # tags: rfd:intrigue
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:11Z (RFD66606-2493) 'Drive the relay's state machine with four clients whose clocks are offset, skewed and
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:12Z (RFD66606-2493) 'jittered, for 19,200 ticks. It passes when no honest frame is refused and every flood frame is.
 # tags: rfd:exit
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:13Z (RFD66606-2493) 'a zone relay only routes
 # tags: rfd:details-title, rfd:no-final-newline
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:14Z (RFD66606-2493) '- A zone relay hands each member's two frames to the other members as they came. It does not
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:15Z (RFD66606-2493) '  simulate, decode, compress or judge, and it holds no key (operator, 2026-11-13).
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:16Z (RFD66606-2493) '- A half of a slot is open again 5 ticks after the frame it last took, counted on the relay's
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:17Z (RFD66606-2493) '  own clock from that frame and from nothing else. A frame that comes sooner is counted and
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:18Z (RFD66606-2493) '  not stored, so a flood makes the relay do less.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:19Z (RFD66606-2493) '- The half of a datagram is the socket it arrived on: first frames go to one port and second
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:20Z (RFD66606-2493) '  frames to the next. Nothing is added to a frame and nothing travels beside it.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:21Z (RFD66606-2493) '- The relay is plain C with no heap and no engine, held to a model in SafeGDScript by
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:22Z (RFD66606-2493) '  replaying a recorded trace of every call and every answer.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:23Z (RFD66606-2493) '- Liveness is the relay's and safety is not: it can drop or delay, and it cannot forge.
 # tags: rfd:decision
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:24Z (RFD66606-2493) '- RFD66606-2436, presence, the slice this relay serves.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:25Z (RFD66606-2493) '- RFD66606-2443, the entity server it was first built beside, which this narrows.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:26Z (RFD66606-2493) '- RFD66606-2442, the latency budget that is where its tick is going.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:27Z (RFD66606-2493) '- RFD66606-2492, the predictor that makes what it carries smaller.
 # tags: rfd:related
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:28Z (RFD66606-2493) 'Where it lives
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:29Z (RFD66606-2493) 'The parts are repositories of their own in our organisation, each started anew on 2026-11-13.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:30Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:31Z (RFD66606-2493) '- The model is the zone router guest, interactor-zone-router-guest: `router.sgd` and the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:32Z (RFD66606-2493) '  script that writes its trace.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:33Z (RFD66606-2493) '- The relay is transport-zone-relay: `src/zone_relay.c` is the state machine, `src/zone_net.c`
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:34Z (RFD66606-2493) '  puts it on two sockets and a 64 Hz tick, and `src/zone_load.c` is the load generator.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:35Z (RFD66606-2493) '- The gates that run four clients through the model, with a planted zone, sender and viewer,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:36Z (RFD66606-2493) '  are in interactor-presence-gates, beside the ledger of what each rung moved.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:37Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:38Z (RFD66606-2493) 'The rule and what it replaced
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:39Z (RFD66606-2493) 'The rule before opened slot `s` where the relay's `now % 6` was 0, 1, 3 or 4. That put the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:40Z (RFD66606-2493) 'senders on different ticks, which is good, and tied a sender's turn to the relay's clock,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:41Z (RFD66606-2493) 'which is not. The rule now needs no shared clock. Five ticks and not six, so that a frame one
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:42Z (RFD66606-2493) 'tick early is still taken. A flood gets at most six frames through in five intervals.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:43Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:44Z (RFD66606-2493) 'Clients still send on different ticks of the six. That is a courtesy that spreads arrivals,
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:45Z (RFD66606-2493) 'kept by the clients. The relay enforces no slot.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:46Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:47Z (RFD66606-2493) 'What was measured
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:48Z (RFD66606-2493) 'The same fixed sequence was given to the rule in use and to the old rule, kept as a planted
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:49Z (RFD66606-2493) 'build. Four clients start at different moments, run 1,000 and 100 parts in a million fast and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:50Z (RFD66606-2493) 'slow, and arrive up to 0.4 of a tick early or late.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:51Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:52Z (RFD66606-2493) '| Rule | Honest frames sent | Honest frames refused | Flood frames refused |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:53Z (RFD66606-2493) '| --- | --- | --- | --- |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:54Z (RFD66606-2493) '| open 5 ticks after the last frame | 25,602 | 0 | 128 of 128 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:55Z (RFD66606-2493) '| open on a fixed tick of the relay's clock | 25,602 | 1,894 | 128 of 128 |
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:56Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:57Z (RFD66606-2493) 'On sockets, four client threads on one machine: 0 honest frames refused of 960 over three
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:58Z (RFD66606-2493) 'runs, where the first run under the old rule refused 7 of 320. A Linux runner printed the same
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:00:59Z (RFD66606-2493) 'figures as the development machine.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:00Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:01Z (RFD66606-2493) 'On Linux the relay reads up to 32 datagrams in one call and sends the frames of one tick in
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:02Z (RFD66606-2493) 'batched calls, and falls back to one call a datagram elsewhere. On a rented machine with the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:03Z (RFD66606-2493) 'loopback and the same traffic, at 256 people, the median tick fell from 1.97e-3 s to
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:04Z (RFD66606-2493) '1.64e-3 s and a datagram sent cost 4.6e-6 s where it cost 5.5e-6 s. A later run at 256
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:05Z (RFD66606-2493) 'people read a median tick of 1.77e-3 s and a 99th percentile of 2.44e-3 s, under the 4e-3 s
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:06Z (RFD66606-2493) 'budget of RFD66606-2442, with 4.9e-6 s a datagram and no overrun. At 1,024 people the
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:07Z (RFD66606-2493) 'loader and the relay shared two cores and the 99th percentile passed the budget.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:08Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:09Z (RFD66606-2493) 'Gates and controls
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:10Z (RFD66606-2493) 'Each gate prints a result line, and each control plants a defect that must be caught.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:11Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:12Z (RFD66606-2493) '- Trace: the C relay answers every one of 1,469 recorded calls as the model did. Controls:
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:13Z (RFD66606-2493) '  five planted models, each of which must fail at the record where it first differs.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:14Z (RFD66606-2493) '- Opaque: the relay's source touches a frame only to store it and to send it. Control: one
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:15Z (RFD66606-2493) '  planted read of a frame byte.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:16Z (RFD66606-2493) '- Clocks: the table above. Controls: the old rule, and a flood.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:17Z (RFD66606-2493) '- Sockets: no viewer gets a frame that differs from what was sent, or its own, or one from
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:18Z (RFD66606-2493) '  the socket of the other half. Controls: a relay that sends from the wrong socket, and 6 ms
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:19Z (RFD66606-2493) '  of planted work in every tick, which must move the median tick by at least 5 ms.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:20Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:21Z (RFD66606-2493) 'What it does not guarantee
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:22Z (RFD66606-2493) '- It can drop or delay, and honest clients cannot route around it.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:23Z (RFD66606-2493) '- A relay that is handed one pair key can alter a frame for that one viewer under a valid
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:24Z (RFD66606-2493) '  tag. The honest majority then names that viewer and not the relay.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:25Z (RFD66606-2493) '- A person here is an address. The home server's member table, and a datagram refused
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:26Z (RFD66606-2493) '  because its address was never named, arrive with the transport step.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:27Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:28Z (RFD66606-2493) 'What is not known
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:29Z (RFD66606-2493) '- The cost of one datagram on a real network. The development machine charges about 4e-4 s
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:30Z (RFD66606-2493) '  for a loopback datagram, so its times compare one run with the next and nothing else. The
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:31Z (RFD66606-2493) '  Linux figures above are loopback too, with the load generator beside the relay.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:32Z (RFD66606-2493) '- Whether a ring of submissions on Linux beats batched calls. None was built. A send costs
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:33Z (RFD66606-2493) '  about 3.4e-6 s at 75, 300 and 1,200 bytes alike, so a smaller frame saves time only when it
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:34Z (RFD66606-2493) '  also means fewer datagrams.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:35Z (RFD66606-2493) '- How the relay shares a viewer's frames among more than four people. The frame budget and
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:36Z (RFD66606-2493) '  its levels of detail by Morton prefix depth are a later rung.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:37Z (RFD66606-2493) '
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:38Z (RFD66606-2493) 'The problem
 # tags: rfd:details-heading
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

2026-11-13T00:01:39Z (RFD66606-2493) 'The relay had been made blind to frames and was still not blind to time.
 # tags: rfd:details
 Text:RFD2493  1 LINE
 Text:Written

